WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.730
We're so honored to welcome a real-life hometown hero

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.070
right here to the desk.

3
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.350
She's a Drew-gooder and she's from Philly

4
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.110
who spent 30 years educating and cultivating the kids

5
00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.400 line:15%
who grow up here.

6
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.580 line:15%
This year, in such a challenging time for students,

7
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.550 line:15%
she launched Cooks with Books,

8
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.210 line:15%
a virtual experience that pairs cooking with literacy.

9
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.700
This is so up our alley.

10
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.390
Take a look at this.

11
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.130
So we're making petite peach pies and I already made some,

12
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.280
they're already delicious.

13
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.220
I tried them, I'm going to show you them later.

14
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.860
But I'm also reading a super fun book today.

15
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.420
This is called, The Night I Followed the Dog.

16
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.330
Now please give a hometown welcome to a true Philly hero,

17
00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.309
It's Marie Lambert. (audience clapping)

18
00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:47.142
Yes!

19
00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.240
Thank you so much.

20
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.880
I am so excited to be here.

21
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.370
This is just awesome.

22
00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:58.320
I mean, you really like as a teacher and a nurturer,

23
00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.120
what happened to you in life that, you know,

24
00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.600
set you on a path to care about kids so much?

25
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.420 line:15%
I was born into an educator-rich family.

26
00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.253 line:15%
Really?

27
00:01:11.253 --> 00:01:13.360 line:15%
So my father didn't have a lot of formal education,

28
00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.283 line:15%
but he believed that his children should all be educated.

29
00:01:18.135 --> 00:01:19.470
I want to talk about what you're doing.

30
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.130
Your nonprofit, True Way Youth Empowerment Foundation,

31
00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:24.110
it's been going for a decade now.

32
00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:24.943
Yes.

33
00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:26.100
That's incredible.

34
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.360
What is your mission?

35
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.610
So our mission is to empower, inspire,

36
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.650 line:15%
and enlighten young people to tap into their greatness,

37
00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.500 line:15%
to think outside the box,

38
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.350 line:15%
to be problem solvers and critical thinkers,

39
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:40.200
and to build strong character.

40
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.930
We do a series of games and activities to have them

41
00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:49.930
really work through a problem without getting angry

42
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.550
or using foul language or violence.

43
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.020
They really have to use their minds

44
00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.720
to really think about what they would do

45
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.130
and how they would solve a problem.

46
00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:05.030
Now, the pandemic put a pause on the cause

47
00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.510
and on your conference,

48
00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.720
but you've got a very special plan for this year.

49
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:09.870
Will you tell us about it?

50
00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:14.050
I am so excited because True Way is set to put on

51
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:18.630
the best youth virtual conference ever.

52
00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.590
January, 2022, right?

53
00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:24.010
The Think Outside the Box Conference.

54
00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.900
The content of your character is a theme of it

55
00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.260
and we are set to invite educators and professionals

56
00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.070
in all areas of industry, business, the arts,

57
00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.680
science, health and wellness,

58
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.780
and put on the best virtual conference ever.

59
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.530
Amazing. (audience clapping)

60
00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:43.420
That is so cool.

61
00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:46.080
We are just so inspired by your beautiful work

62
00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.370
for Philly's young people.

63
00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:50.470
So we reached out to our friends at Jada Toys

64
00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:53.890
and they make the B-kind dolls, an eco-friendly line

65
00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.705
that promotes messages of kindness

66
00:02:55.705 --> 00:03:00.030
and inspires kids to be creative and compassionate.

67
00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.100
And they want to recognize you with your kindness

68
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.180
with a $20,000 donation (audience cheering)

69
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.700
to True Way Youth Empowerment Foundation

70
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.202
to help and enable all the work that you do, Marie.

71
00:03:14.202 --> 00:03:17.075
(audience cheering)

72
00:03:17.075 --> 00:03:20.992
(laughs) This is so amazing.

73
00:03:21.842 --> 00:03:23.892
(cheering drowns out speaker)

74
00:03:23.892 --> 00:03:26.271
Oh my gosh, oh my gosh, this is awesome.

75
00:03:26.271 --> 00:03:27.199
Thank you so much!

76
00:03:27.199 --> 00:03:28.157
Thank you!

77
00:03:28.157 --> 00:03:30.040
I don't know what to say.

78
00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.330
I mean, you're molding minds and hearts, Marie.

79
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.810
You're extraordinary.

80
00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:34.740
So here you go.

81
00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.170
Thank you so much.

82
00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.100
Thank you Jada Toys and B-kind dolls.

83
00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.900
And thank you, Marie Lambert, for being here.

84
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.510
Thank you so much for having me.

85
00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.243 line:15%
This was a blast!
(Ross laughing)

86
00:03:46.243 --> 00:03:48.304 line:15%
(audience cheering)

87
00:03:48.304 --> 00:03:49.214 line:15%
Congratulations.

88
00:03:49.214 --> 00:03:50.410 line:15%
Yeah, but this is exciting!

89
00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.793
Thank you so much!

90
00:03:51.793 --> 00:03:53.570
Thank you, I appreciate it.

91
00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:54.660
Well, thank you, Marie.

92
00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:55.740
And thank you, Rossi.

93
00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:57.137
We got to come to Philly!

94
00:03:57.137 --> 00:03:59.178
I know! (cheering)

95
00:03:59.178 --> 00:04:02.595 line:15%
(light, energetic music)

